        "body": "Fathom is a San Francisco-based company, founded in 2020 and publicly traded under the ticker FTHM, that provides an AI-powered meeting notetaker supporting Zoom, Google Meet, and Microsoft Teams calls. The company describes its core product as capturing, transcribing, and summarizing calls automatically, with a free tier for individuals and paid features aimed at teams. Its \"Ask Fathom\" feature allows users to search across meeting content and receive AI-generated summaries tailored to a team's workflow.\n\nBeyond transcription, the product generates action items and call insights that the company says flow automatically into connected tools, including CRM platforms, without requiring manual updates. Fathom also offers AI Scorecards, which the site describes as providing real-time coaching moments and follow-up metrics to help managers evaluate and improve team performance. The product is positioned against competitors including Fireflies, Granola, Gong, Otter, Read AI, ZoomMate, and built-in platform solutions.\n\nThe held facts identify Fathom as a for-profit public company with CIK 0001753162, indicating an SEC registration. No litigation or MCP server records are currently associated with the company in the held facts.",
